An ACL injury is a tear of the anterior cruciate ligament in the knee, often caused by [**Mayo Clinic ACL Injuries Overview**](https://sportsmedicine.mayoclinic.org/condition/acl-injuries/) sudden stops or pivoting. It causes a popping sound, swelling, and instability, frequently requiring surgery and physical therapy to recover.

